WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.360 --> 00:00:03.960
- I'm in Ukraine

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:07.260
and like just about
everybody leaving Kyiv today,

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.950
I spent about 10 hours so far in the car

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.325
and have gotten not that far away.

00:00:12.325 --> 00:00:14.992
(pensive music)

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:21.380
The roads are packed because
the civilian airspace

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:22.734
has been closed.

00:00:22.734 --> 00:00:24.520
(siren wailing)

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:25.980
and there was real chaos

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:28.690
at the the main rail station in Kyiv.

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.330
The bus service, as
far as we had observed,

00:00:31.330 --> 00:00:33.800
was also shut down outta Kyiv.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:37.000
And so going by road,
fleeing by road west,

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.810
is really the only way to go.

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.477
(pensive music)

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:47.610
Many of the people I've been
talking to across Ukraine

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.710
can't even get out of
the cities they're in

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.350
mainly because they they're
afraid to go outside.

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:56.840
They're hearing small arms fire, missiles,

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.720
all sorts of heavy military
action right around them.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:03.290
Some of them feel like they can't leave.

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.750
The gas stations locally
have run outta gas

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:08.470
and they really don't know what to do.

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:12.920
So the folks who are on this
long long drive west outta Kyiv

00:01:12.920 --> 00:01:14.223
are really the lucky ones.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:17.980
People who are fleeing the hostilities

00:01:17.980 --> 00:01:19.750
are mostly going west.

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.780
And they're trying to get
over the borders into Moldova,

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.160
Slovakia, Hungary, or Poland.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:29.160
(quiet chime music)

00:01:51.559 --> 00:01:55.350
You've seen people trying to
get out in all sorts of ways.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.320
We've passed masses of people

00:01:57.320 --> 00:02:00.020
just simply trying to
hitch hike on the highway.

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.580
We've seen people walking
with, with luggage,

00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:06.340
people on bikes, any which way they can.

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:08.050
This is a lengthy process.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.230
And then also once they
do get to the borders

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.205
depending on which country
they're trying to get into,

00:02:13.205 --> 00:02:16.895
the process of getting
through immigration there

00:02:16.895 --> 00:02:19.253
adds many hours on top of that.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:24.740
It's too early to tell
how this is all gonna go

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:26.910
in terms of whether or not we're looking

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.960
at a prolonged refugee crisis

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:32.080
or if there's gonna be stability in Kyiv

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.340
in other cities in the near term.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.344
That doesn't seem likely.

00:02:35.344 --> 00:02:37.844
(quiet music)

